WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.920 --> 00:00:06.560
Freud's theory of psychosexual
development claims that as we grow up we

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:10.880
pass through
five critical phases.

00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:14.320
Our sex drive, which Freud called the
Libido,

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:18.480
focuses in a different erogenous zone at
each phase.

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:27.599
The phases are called Oral, Anal,
Phallic, Latency and Genital.

00:00:27.599 --> 00:00:31.599
If our experience during any of these
phases was traumatic

00:00:31.599 --> 00:00:38.079
we might develop fixations later in life
such as neurosis, dependencies addictions,

00:00:38.079 --> 00:00:41.260
or depression.

00:00:41.260 --> 00:00:43.413
The Oral Phase,
age zero to one.

00:00:43.413 --> 00:00:44.960
In the first year of our

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:47.520
lives
we discover the world through our oral

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:52.879
senses. Our main pleasure comes from
sucking our mother's breast or a bottle.

00:00:52.879 --> 00:00:57.600
The conflict that occurs now is the
weaning from our primary caregiver.

00:00:57.600 --> 00:01:01.440
Hans is weaned off his mother's breast
without trauma.

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:05.199
Ernst's mother stops feeding him within
four months of birth

00:01:05.199 --> 00:01:07.480
which is too early.

00:01:07.480 --> 00:01:08.720
Ida is often left
alone

00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:12.820
crying when she is hungry.

00:01:12.820 --> 00:01:14.799
Hans becomes a healthy and independent

00:01:14.799 --> 00:01:18.400
adult.
Ernst suffers from trauma and develops

00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:22.479
an oral fixation. He tries to compensate for it by chewing

00:01:22.479 --> 00:01:26.720
gum all the time.
Ida spends her entire life looking for

00:01:26.720 --> 00:01:29.439
the oral stimulation she was denied as
an

00:01:29.439 --> 00:01:36.000
infant and therefore develops a
manipulative and addictive personality.

00:01:36.079 --> 00:01:39.220
The a=Anal Phase, age one to three.

00:01:39.220 --> 00:01:41.680
The primary focus of our Libido at this

00:01:41.680 --> 00:01:45.520
age is the control of the bladder and
bowel movements.

00:01:45.520 --> 00:01:49.200
We have to learn how to use the potty.
Han's parents

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:53.520
praise his attempts to use the toilet
and encourage him to learn at his own

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:56.960
pace.
Ernst's parents force potty training on

00:01:56.960 --> 00:02:00.880
him too early
and punish him for mistakes. Ida's

00:02:00.880 --> 00:02:06.320
parents neglect
any efforts at potty training entirely.

00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:11.039
Hans develops a competent personality
and a good and balanced relationship

00:02:11.039 --> 00:02:14.720
with authority.
Ernst develops an anal retentive

00:02:14.720 --> 00:02:18.080
personality.
He becomes an over-controlling and

00:02:18.080 --> 00:02:21.599
stingy adult
with disgust for his own body and a

00:02:21.599 --> 00:02:26.560
tendency to obey authority.
Ida develops an anal expulsive

00:02:26.560 --> 00:02:30.319
personality.
She becomes messy disorganized

00:02:30.319 --> 00:02:36.879
inconsiderate of other people's feelings
and rebellious against authority.

00:02:36.879 --> 00:02:40.320
The Phallic Phase, age three to six.

00:02:40.320 --> 00:02:43.200
Our Libido now turns to the genitals as

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:46.560
we discover the differences between the
female and the male

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:52.000
gender. The boy's conflict in this phase
occurs as a rivalry with their father,

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:57.440
also called the 'Oedipus Complex'. Ernst
and Hands desire to possess their mother

00:02:57.440 --> 00:03:00.560
and fantasize about getting rid of their
father

00:03:00.560 --> 00:03:04.000
But they know that their father is
stronger and fear being

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:07.040
punished for their desire. Freud called
this

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:14.159
'Castration Anxiety'. Ida experiences
'Penis Envy'. She believes that a penis is

00:03:14.159 --> 00:03:19.840
the key to power and domination
and also wants one.

00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:23.280
Han's father was very present during
that phase.

00:03:23.280 --> 00:03:27.920
Later, Hans resolves this conflict by
identifying strongly with him.

00:03:27.920 --> 00:03:34.560
He learns to take on a male role. As an
adult he respects both genders. Ernst,

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:39.360
whose father was absent during that
phase, fails to develop a strong sense of

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:42.879
manhood.
He has a mother fixation and is not sure

00:03:42.879 --> 00:03:46.959
about his sexuality.
He also tends to be aggressive towards

00:03:46.959 --> 00:03:49.840
women and
constantly needs to compete with other

00:03:49.840 --> 00:03:54.080
men. Ida,
like all women, maintains her penis envy

00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:58.239
for the rest of her life
which in her case causes an inferiority

00:03:58.239 --> 00:04:02.000
complex towards men.

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:05.620
Latent Phase, age seven to thirteen.

00:04:05.620 --> 00:04:08.080
In this phase our Libido is suppressed

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:11.760
as our sexual energy is being sublimed
into developing

00:04:11.760 --> 00:04:17.359
life skills. Our Superego strengthens
and we strongly identify with social

00:04:17.359 --> 00:04:21.280
values,
same-sex heroes, and friends.

00:04:21.280 --> 00:04:25.840
Hans follows many hobbies. Ernst loves
learning at school,

00:04:25.840 --> 00:04:30.880
and Ida makes lots of new girlfriends.

00:04:30.880 --> 00:04:35.600
There is no real conflict in this phase.
All three of them benefit for the rest

00:04:35.600 --> 00:04:38.000
of their lives from the skills they
developed

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:41.700
during latency.

00:04:41.700 --> 00:04:44.400
The Genital Phase, puberty to death.

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:47.759
Once we reach puberty our libido starts
to become

00:04:47.759 --> 00:04:52.080
active again and we develop an interest
in sexual partners.

00:04:52.080 --> 00:04:57.199
Hans, Ida and Ernst face the challenge
of balancing the sexual desires of the

00:04:57.199 --> 00:05:00.080
Id
and the needs of the Superego to obey

00:05:00.080 --> 00:05:04.240
social norms.
The development of a strong Ego helps to

00:05:04.240 --> 00:05:08.240
find a compromise between the two.

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:12.160
Hans, who has experienced a childhood
without much trauma,

00:05:12.160 --> 00:05:16.560
succeeds in building a strong Ego. He is
disciplined at work,

00:05:16.560 --> 00:05:19.680
has a loving relationship. and a
fulfilled sex

00:05:19.680 --> 00:05:23.759
life. Ernst's Ego is weaker than his
superego

00:05:23.759 --> 00:05:27.199
he obeys norms and authorities and as a
result

00:05:27.199 --> 00:05:32.240
suppresses his desires which leads to
the development of perversions.

00:05:32.240 --> 00:05:38.320
Ida has a weak Ego and a weak Superego.
Her sexual needs are more important than

00:05:38.320 --> 00:05:44.160
social norms or other people's feelings.
She is egoistic and feels no guilt for

00:05:44.160 --> 00:05:48.160
breaking the law or hurting others.

00:05:48.639 --> 00:05:52.000
To understand the theory we need to see
it in the context of

00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:56.479
Freud's famous work on the unconscious.
By acknowledging that we have a

00:05:56.479 --> 00:05:59.840
subconscious.
He also implied that we store memories

00:05:59.840 --> 00:06:03.600
of early childhood
and other experiences without even

00:06:03.600 --> 00:06:06.960
realizing it.
These past experiences then

00:06:06.960 --> 00:06:12.560
unconsciously influence our behavior on
a daily basis.

00:06:12.800 --> 00:06:16.400
Freud claimed that our mind operates in
three spheres

00:06:16.400 --> 00:06:20.000
which we can imagine as a submarine. The Unconscious

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:25.440
level operates the Id.
The Preconscious level operates the

00:06:25.440 --> 00:06:30.479
Superego. The Conscious and Preconscious levels

00:06:30.479 --> 00:06:35.680
operate our Ego.
Young children are driven by the Id and

00:06:35.680 --> 00:06:40.880
demand immediate satisfaction.
At around age seven we begin to develop a

00:06:40.880 --> 00:06:43.759
Superego and want to become good moral

00:06:43.759 --> 00:06:48.160
citizens and please
others. The Ego is formed with

00:06:48.160 --> 00:06:54.400
adolescence
to balance the two forces.

00:06:54.400 --> 00:06:58.759
Sigmund Shlomo Freud was an Austrian
neurologist and the founder of

00:06:58.759 --> 00:07:04.080
Psychoanalysis. Freud theorized that the
Unconscious would remember and store

00:07:04.080 --> 00:07:08.160
all our experiences later they pop up
from time to time

00:07:08.160 --> 00:07:13.120
through dreams and associative thoughts.
By revealing traumatic memories and

00:07:13.120 --> 00:07:17.759
desires through conversation
we can free ourselves from our neuroses

00:07:17.759 --> 00:07:23.520
and live a more healthy and fulfilled
life. He recommended we should not strive

00:07:23.520 --> 00:07:28.000
to eliminate our complexes
but to get into accord with them. They

00:07:28.000 --> 00:07:33.520
are legitimately what directs
our conduct in the world.

00:07:33.599 --> 00:07:38.080
What do you think about this theory and
the practice of psychoanalysis?

00:07:38.080 --> 00:07:41.919
Is there some truth in it? Do we have an
unconscious?

00:07:41.919 --> 00:07:46.160
If so does it really store all our
childhood experiences

00:07:46.160 --> 00:07:50.479
and influence our behavior as adults?
